1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,903
A Signal Set turns readings into a decision:

2
00:00:02,953 --> 00:00:05,386
Yes, No, or Unknown, with the reason.

3
00:00:05,815 --> 00:00:09,678
Here's a setup many traders look for: a pullback in an uptrend.

4
00:00:09,728 --> 00:00:12,972
The main trend is up, but price has dipped in the short term.

5
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:16,408
Add the My Trend Group we built in the last video.

6
00:00:16,849 --> 00:00:19,453
Add a single signal too: Stochastic,

7
00:00:19,503 --> 00:00:22,695
which shows where the latest close sits in its recent range,

8
00:00:22,715 --> 00:00:25,478
from zero at the low to a hundred at the high.

9
00:00:25,916 --> 00:00:29,267
Now the decision. Line one: My Trend is Bullish.

10
00:00:29,317 --> 00:00:32,881
Line two: Stochastic is at most thirty, a short-term dip.

11
00:00:38,917 --> 00:00:41,222
Both lines must hold for a Yes.

12
00:00:41,272 --> 00:00:44,346
For more flexible rules, you can add "any of" boxes.

13
00:00:44,784 --> 00:00:48,583
Yes means every line holds. No means at least one fails.

14
00:00:48,633 --> 00:00:52,815
Unknown means something needed is missing, and Lattice never fills it in.

15
00:00:53,246 --> 00:00:56,981
The description reads your rule back in plain words. Save it,

16
00:00:57,031 --> 00:00:59,165
and it's ready to scan in Prism.

17
00:01:02,143 --> 00:01:06,603
Why it helps: instead of flicking through charts looking for dips in strong trends,

18
00:01:06,653 --> 00:01:10,196
you get a clear Yes or No for every asset, with its reason.
